    id: "drill-qa-003", kind: "qa", theme: "intro", level: "mid", seconds: 60,
    q: "What part of your current role takes up most of your time?",
    sample: "Honestly, most of my week goes into integration work and production support. We have about twelve services, and the order flow touches payment, inventory, and shipping, so a lot of my time is spent tracing requests across them and fixing edge cases. I probably spend two days a week on code, one day on reviews and design discussions, and the rest on incidents or answering questions from product and operations. It is not glamorous, but it taught me how systems actually fail. I have been trying to reduce that support load by adding better metrics and runbooks. Last quarter we cut the number of repeat incidents by about thirty percent, which gave me more time for design work.",
